<title>CANADA: Caledonia and BHP in Zambian deal.</title>
<headline>Caledonia and BHP in Zambian deal.</headline>
<dateline>OAKVILLE, Ontario 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caledonia Mining Corp said on Thursday it agreed with Broken Hill Proprietary Co Ltd subsidiary BHP Minerals International Exploration Inc to search for minerals at Caledonia's Mulonga Plains property in western Zambia.</p>
<p>The two companies said they would undertake a reconnaissance sampling program to search for gold and minerals on the property, located adjacent to the diamond producing regions of Angola.</p>
<p>Caledonia said that BHP must notify Caledonia by October 1, 1997 if it wishes to form a joint venture partnership on the Mulonga property, which is 100 percent owned by Caledonia.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
